CART 470 - A SONG FOR MY MOTHER - Learning Contract


Thesis/ Project Focus
A Song for My Mother is a tapestry-of-ceramic-beads project that reflects the effects on Indigenous victims of forced adoption and institutionalized family separation. This project materializes survivors’ voices by embedding sound into the work.

How do we design a system that stores people’s voices through ceramics? What does it truly  mean for ceramic to remember a voice? 

Thesis/Project Outcome
Our mission is to prototype a device, object, or method for embedding those voices within the ceramic. From coding to electronics to 3D printing and sensors, multiple options are being considered to make this feasible. 


Knowledge Base/Fields/ Domains/ Keywords
Sensors, survivors, storytelling, ceramic, voices, remembering, exploration, 

